Phase 2 branch diverged from master before Phase 1 (attribute schemas) was merged, causing a conflict in `openEditModal()` where both branches modified the same region around `updateTypeFields`/`updateAttributeFields`.

### Conflict

Master added `updateAttributeFields(cat, sub, existingAttrs)` immediately before the overlay display line. This branch inserted the built-in library search clearing block in the same location. Git couldn't auto-resolve.

### Resolution

Keep both — master's attribute schema call and the branch's search field clearing:

```js
updateAttributeFields(cat, sub, existingAttrs);

// Clear the built-in library search field
const builtinInput = document.getElementById('builtin-search-input');
if (builtinInput) {
  builtinInput.value = '';
  const builtinResults = document.getElementById('builtin-search-results');
  if (builtinResults) { builtinResults.style.display = 'none'; builtinResults.innerHTML = ''; }
}

document.getElementById('overlay-edit').style.display = '';
```

Proper merge commit with both parents so GitHub recognizes master is incorporated and the PR is fast-forward mergeable.

